# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables. Copy to `.env` for local work; set the same values in
# the host's build environment for production. Astro reads them at BUILD time,
# so changing one needs a rebuild.
#
# Everything here is `PUBLIC_`, meaning it is compiled into the pages and
# visible to anyone who views source. Never put a secret in this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where enquiry forms send their submissions. A URL that accepts a POST of
# JSON — Formspree, Netlify Forms, a CRM webhook, a Zapier/Make hook, or the
# IDX provider's lead capture.
#
# UNTIL THIS IS SET, no form claims to have sent anything. Submitting shows the
# visitor their own answers with a prefilled email link to Martin and MaryEllen
# and both direct numbers, so nothing is lost and nothing is faked.
#
# The browser posts to this directly, so the URL itself must not be a
# credential. A provider that needs an API key needs a server-side relay.
# See CONTENT_PENDING.md 6.1.
PUBLIC_LEAD_FORM_ENDPOINT=

# Show the sample listings and developments in a production build. Defaults to
# on in `astro dev` and off in `astro build`; `npm run build:demo` sets it.
# Never set this to true for the live site — the sample records are badged, but
# they are not the client's inventory.
PUBLIC_DEMO_CONTENT=
